Task: Deterministic tie-break and complexity guard

Changes:
- _select_best now uses exact cost equality (no tolerance) and returns the
  first minimal index; because the grid is lexicographic, this is the
  lexicographically smallest optimal point.
- mitigate() raises ValueError if any cost is NaN/inf; exact_mitigate() does
  the same per point, with an actionable message.
- Grid size is validated in __init__ against MAX_GRID_POINTS (1,000,000).

Tests: p2 plateau resolves to the smallest p2 for both solvers; a monkeypatched
cap rejects oversized grids and accepts a fitting one; repeated runs are
deterministic; NaN predictions are rejected.

Files: surrogate_xapps/cmc.py, tests/test_cmc.py
